    <briefdescription>
<para>An exemplar links a specific trace context to a metric observation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Exemplars are stored on histogram metrics and emitted in the Prometheus OpenMetrics text format alongside the histogram summary output:</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="preprocessor">#<sp/>TYPE<sp/>some_latency_ms<sp/>summary</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">some_latency_ms{quantile=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;0.99&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">}<sp/>42.0<sp/>#<sp/>{traceID=</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;3e561c74cee40c12&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">}<sp/>42.0<sp/>1712000000.000</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>At most one exemplar is retained per metric series (last-write-wins).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>observeHistogramWithExemplar() </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
